WEBVTT

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:17.520
What is that?

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:20.040
- Look at that!
- That is cool!

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:22.080
Come on!

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:24.760
I don't think he's a dentist.

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:39.800
We've been working on this
for a while.

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:42.520
It's a anti-gravity serum.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:51.280
I meant to close that.
He'll be all right, I'm sure.

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:54.280
- Do the effects wear off?
- So far,

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:56.280
no. No, they don't.

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:00.720
And here, of course,
is the new weapon you ordered.

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:05.240
No, no.

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:09.000
I said "dart gun," not... Okay.

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:12.200
Oh, yes. 'Cause I was wondering

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:14.800
under what circumstances
would we use this?

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:16.280
But, anyway.

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:19.640
What I really wanted
to show you was this.

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:27.200
Now those are cookie robots!

00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:31.400
La, la, la, la
I love unicorns

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:35.000
What are you doing here?
I told you to stay in the kitchen!

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:37.640
We got bored. What is this place?

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:39.400
Can I drink this?

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:41.840
Do you want to explode?

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:44.400
Gru!

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:46.360
Get back in the kitchen!

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:48.480
- Will you play with us?
- No.

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:51.000
- Why?
- Because I'm busy.

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:52.600
Doing what?

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:55.480
Okay, okay, you got me.

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:58.200
The dentist thing is more
of a hobby.

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:01.080
In real life, I am a spy.

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:04.600
And it is top secret,
and you may not tell anybody,

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:06.680
- because if you do...
- What does this do?

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:11.480
Hey!

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:13.680
My unicorn!

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.600
You have to fix it.

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:18.200
Fix it? Look,
it has been disintegrated.

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:20.760
By definition, it cannot be fixed.

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:27.880
That's freaking me out.
What is she doing?

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:31.040
She's gonna hold her breath
until she gets a new one.

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:35.600
It is just a toy. Now stop it!

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:39.840
Okay, okay! I'll fix it!

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:42.120
Tim! Mark! Phil!

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:45.880
This is very important.

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:49.320
You have to get the little girl
a new unicorn toy.

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:56.880
Hey, hey, hey! A toy!

00:02:58.040 --> 00:03:00.080
Go, and hurry!

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:01.280
What are those?

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:04.400
They are my cousins.

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:06.680
Jerry! Stuart!

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:10.600
Watch them,
and keep them away from me, please.

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:29.440
- Wow!
- Wow!

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:32.960
It was your cousin's idea.

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:34.400
What?

00:04:34.760 --> 00:04:36.200
Okay, bedtime.

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:40.760
Not you two!

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:46.760
Okey-dokey. Beddie-bye.
All tucked in. Sweet dreams.

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:50.360
Just so you know,

00:04:50.440 --> 00:04:52.320
you're never gonna be my dad.

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:54.880
I think I can live with that.

00:04:56.480 --> 00:04:58.240
Are these beds made out of bombs?

00:04:58.760 --> 00:05:02.760
Yes, but they are very old
and highly unlikely to blow up.

00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:05.600
But try not to toss and turn.

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:06.760
Cool.

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:10.720
- Will you read us a bedtime story?
- No.

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:13.760
But we can't go to sleep
without a bedtime story.

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:17.280
Well, then it's going to be
a long night for you, isn't it?

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:21.560
So, good night, sleep tight,
and don't let the bed bugs bite.

00:05:21.640 --> 00:05:25.360
Because there are literally
thousands of them.

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:29.400
And there's probably
something in your closet.

00:05:30.920 --> 00:05:33.000
He's just kidding, Agnes.

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:56.160
It's beautiful.

